# forge/fit/lacing: side lacing (HOMESPUN, Marsh; 28.3): a cord (accent) zigzagging down each side seam of the coat,
# period 4, connected diagonally.
# FORGE-MARKS, forge i2 (tools: emb_P2c/forge/areas/FORGE-MARKS/tools2/mk2.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# FITTING (`overlay fit.<v>`): P-box fits (`tags tile overlay fit`, `on-region P`: the largest <w>x<h> view that fits
# the piece's panel, centred: bosses, star rivets, knotwork), seam fittings (`on-region N`, a periodic tile on the seams
# the cut marks: rivets), or plane tiles (`on-slot:<slot>`, as a cut: studs, scored lines, the inlay band, lacing).
# Cells as the limb tile's (region tiles) or the cut tile's (plane tiles).
use person
role overlay fit.lacing
tags tile overlay on-slot:cloth3
legend + ink 3
legend ^ ink 4
legend : ink 1
legend = ink 0
legend O metal2 2
legend n accent 1
legend o accent 2
legend p accent 3

# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i2) the cord drawn as a darker thread of the coat itself (ink 1: its step less one), not in the
# accent: the blind panel read the red accent zigzag on the buff T1 coat as "a rash or blood"; the side seams read as
# laced at 3x and as a quiet seam at 1x.
view D key rest origin 7 0
|...............
|...............
|...:......:....
|....:......:...
|...:......:....
|....:......:...
|...:......:....
|....:......:...
